      "lineRange": [511, 559],
      "summary": "Command-line front end for the replay auditor, cleaning up its ephemeral staging roots and exiting non-zero on divergence or a fail-closed precondition.",
      "tags": ["cli", "entry-point", "argument-parsing"],
      "complexity": "moderate"
    },

    {
      "id": "file:runner/graph_projector.py",
      "type": "file",
      "name": "graph_projector.py",
      "filePath": "runner/graph_projector.py",
      "summary": "The docs-to-graph projector: scans durable Tier 4 phase and gate state and mirrors it into the vault as derived, read-only phase_gate_state nodes so the Obsidian dashboards reflect run state. It is deterministic and idempotent, writes only its own owned vault folder, and enforces that the two sync directions never write the same docs path or vault folder.",
      "tags": ["projector", "graph-substrate", "mirror", "idempotent", "cli"],
      "complexity": "complex",
      "languageNotes": "The mirror is deliberately one-way and derived: it carries no fresh timestamp and the gate evaluator never reads the vault, so projecting cannot change a gate outcome or input freshness."
    },
